[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":135},"routes/item",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10},"item",{"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":-5,"_20":21,"_22":23,"_24":25,"_26":27,"_28":27,"_29":30,"_31":32,"_33":34,"_35":36,"_37":38,"_39":40,"_41":-5,"_42":43,"_44":45,"_46":47,"_48":49,"_50":51,"_52":53,"_54":36,"_55":56,"_57":58,"_59":36,"_60":61},"expiresAt",1795567286000,"id","puwa8poiznezf6mv38zskg8oz","title","AWS Europe (Spain) Region 获西班牙 Difusión Limitada 与 NATO Restricted 认证","originalTitle","AWS achieves Spain’s national Limited Distribution (Difusión Limitada) and NATO Restricted accreditation in the AWS Europe (Spain) Region","summary","AWS Europe (Spain) Region 获西班牙 Difusión Limitada 与 NATO Restricted 认证，可承载对应级别的涉密工作负载。","reason","source",{"_73":134},"links",{"_61":133},"publishedAt","2026-11-24T17:38:00.000Z","discoveredAt","2026-11-24T18:02:35.467Z","timelineAt","category","policy","tags",[128,129,130,131,132],"score",46,"selected",false,"channel","news","story",{"_82":83,"_13":84},"x","readingMode","full","author","Borja Larrumbide","body",{"_124":-5,"_61":125,"_126":-5,"_127":36},"outline",[85,86,87,88,89,90,91,92,93,94,95,96],"relatedStories",[81],"topics",[68,69,70,71],"indexable","markdownAvailable",true,"group",{"_62":63,"_64":65,"_66":67},"hasTranslation","bodyLanguage","original","factId","fvh-HwyGERZM","reportCount",1,"additionalSourceCount",0,{"_72":79,"_73":80},{"_72":77,"_73":78},{"_72":75,"_73":76},{"_72":30,"_73":74},"slug","name","政策法规","compliance","合规与标准","cloud-native","云与原生","supply-chain","供应链安全",{"_82":83,"_13":84},"publicId","cd352667-cce2-4583-8157-63a47028ea01","AWS西班牙区域获涉密信息认证",{"_11":122,"_98":123,"_99":103},{"_11":120,"_98":121,"_99":103},{"_11":118,"_98":119,"_99":103},{"_11":116,"_98":117,"_99":103},{"_11":114,"_98":115,"_99":103},{"_11":112,"_98":113,"_99":103},{"_11":110,"_98":111,"_99":103},{"_11":108,"_98":109,"_99":103},{"_11":106,"_98":107,"_99":103},{"_11":104,"_98":105,"_99":103},{"_11":101,"_98":102,"_99":103},{"_11":97,"_98":45,"_99":100},"sec-12","text","level",3,"sec-11","Cómo empezar",2,"sec-10","Por qué es importante para los clientes","sec-9","¿Qué es NATO Restricted?","sec-8","¿Cuál es el marco español de información clasificada?","sec-7","Qué abarca","sec-6","AWS obtiene la acreditación Difusión Limitada y NATO Restricted en la Región AWS","sec-5","How to get started","sec-4","Why this matters to customers","sec-3","What is NATO Restricted?","sec-2","What is Spain’s classified information framework?","sec-1","What this covers","zh","<p><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/security/aws-achieves-spains-national-limited-distribution-difusion-limitada-and-nato-restricted-accreditation-in-the-aws-europe-spain-region/#Spanish-version\">Spanish version »</a></p><p><span><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/\">Amazon Web Services (AWS)</a></span> is pleased to announce that AWS has achieved Spain’s national Limited Distribution (“Difusión Limitada”) and NATO Restricted accreditation for the AWS Europe (Spain) Region. The Difusión Limitada and NATO Restricted accreditation was granted by the Spanish Delegated Authority for the Security of Classified Information, the Secretary of State Director of Spain’s <span><a href=\"https://www.cni.es/en/\">Centro Nacional de Inteligencia (CNI)</a></span>. The <span><a href=\"https://www.ccn-cert.cni.es/en/\">Centro Criptológico Nacional (CCN)</a></span> and the <span><a href=\"https://www.cni.es/en/ons\">Oficina Nacional de Seguridad (ONS)</a></span> are working bodies of the CNI, which audited AWS against the <span><a href=\"https://www.ccn-cert.cni.es/es/guias-de-acceso-publico-ccn-stic/7358-ccn-stic-004-manejo-de-informacion-con-clasificacion-difusion-limitada-o-equivalente-en-nube-publica/file.html\">CCN-STIC-004</a></span> policy and the applicable ONS requirements.</p><p>With this milestone, AWS becomes the first cloud provider to be accredited under NATO Restricted level, and the first to be accredited for Difusión Limitada in the AWS Europe (Spain) Region. In Spain, this was a double achievement: AWS first met the national Difusión Limitada requirements and then, in addition to this national methodology, achieved the NATO Restricted accreditation by incorporating the requirements of NATO Directive 32. This demonstrates our continued commitment to helping the public sector, defense, and NATO-affiliated customers run sensitive workloads in the cloud while meeting the highest applicable national and international security requirements.</p><h2 id=\"sec-1\">What this covers</h2><p>The Difusión Limitada and NATO Restricted accreditation by the CNI confirms that the AWS system in the AWS Europe (Spain) Region meets the procedural and security requirements for handling classified information up to the Difusión Limitada and NATO Restricted level.</p><h2 id=\"sec-2\">What is Spain’s classified information framework?</h2><p>Spain’s framework for protecting national classified information is administered by the ONS and the CCN, under the CNI. In 2026, Spain established the framework that enables handling of Difusión Limitada information in the commercial public cloud, under which this accreditation was granted. The accreditation builds on the AWS <span><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/esquema-nacional-de-seguridad/\">ENS High certification</a></span> and the CCN’s <span><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/ccn-stic/\">IT Product and Service Catalogue</a></span> (CPSTIC) qualifications. The scope of the accreditation covers the CPSTIC-qualified services and all AWS services certified under ENS High (see the <span><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/services-in-scope/ENS-High/\">list of AWS services in scope for ENS High</a></span>). Only the services within this scope that are qualified or certified under the CCN framework (CPSTIC and ENS High) and run in the AWS Europe (Spain) Region can be used for Difusión Limitada and NATO Restricted workloads.</p><h2 id=\"sec-3\">What is NATO Restricted?</h2><p>NATO Directive 32 establishes the security requirements for handling NATO Restricted information in public cloud, and is the directive referenced by Spain’s <span><a href=\"https://www.ccn-cert.cni.es/es/guias-de-acceso-publico-ccn-stic/7358-ccn-stic-004-manejo-de-informacion-con-clasificacion-difusion-limitada-o-equivalente-en-nube-publica/file.html\">CCN-STIC-004</a></span> policy.</p><h2 id=\"sec-4\">Why this matters to customers</h2><p>Public sector and defense organizations in Spain can use the AWS Europe (Spain) Region for national Difusión Limitada classified workloads and for NATO Restricted workloads. Under the shared responsibility model, customers that want to process classified information in the AWS Europe (Spain) Region engage the CCN and ONS to accredit their own systems, building on the AWS accreditation.</p><h2 id=\"sec-5\">How to get started</h2><p>National security and defense customers may build on the <span><a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/solutions/trusted-secure-enclaves-on-aws/\">AWS Trusted Secure Enclave, Sensitive Edition (TSE-SE)</a></span> to design a cloud architecture for their sensitive workloads. Accreditation documentation is available to eligible customers through <span><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/artifact/\">AWS Artifact</a></span>. Customers can also work with their AWS account teams to understand how the Difusión Limitada and NATO Restricted accreditation, and TSE-SE apply to their use cases.</p><p>To learn more about AWS compliance in Spain, see the <span><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/esquema-nacional-de-seguridad/\">AWS ENS compliance page</a></span> and the <span><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/programs/\">AWS Compliance Programs</a></span> page.</p><p>For more details see <span><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/dl-spain-and-nato-restricted-service-approval/\">AWS NATO Restricted and Difusión Limitada for AWS Europe (Spain) Region web page</a></span><br> &nbsp;</p><hr><p>Spanish version</p><h2 id=\"sec-6\">AWS obtiene la acreditación Difusión Limitada y NATO Restricted en la Región AWS Europa (España)</h2><p>Amazon Web Services (AWS) se complace en anunciar que ha obtenido la acreditación nacional de España “Difusión Limitada” y la acreditación NATO Restricted para la Región AWS Europa (España). La acreditación Difusión Limitada y NATO Restricted ha sido concedida por la Autoridad Delegada para la Seguridad de la Información Clasificada de España, la Secretaria de Estado Directora del <span><a href=\"https://www.cni.es/\">Centro Nacional de Inteligencia (CNI)</a></span>. El <span><a href=\"https://www.ccn-cert.cni.es/\">Centro Criptológico Nacional (CCN)</a></span>, y la <a href=\"https://www.cni.es/oficina-nacional-de-seguridad\">Oficina Nacional de Seguridad (ONS)</a>, son órganos de trabajo del CNI, que auditaron a AWS conforme a la política <span><a href=\"https://www.ccn-cert.cni.es/es/guias-de-acceso-publico-ccn-stic/7358-ccn-stic-004-manejo-de-informacion-con-clasificacion-difusion-limitada-o-equivalente-en-nube-publica/file.html\">CCN-STIC-004</a></span> y a los requisitos aplicables de la ONS.</p><p>Con este hito, AWS se convierte en el primer proveedor cloud acreditado en el nivel NATO Restricted, y en el primero acreditado para Difusión Limitada en la Región AWS Europa (España). En España ha sido un doble logro: AWS cumplió primero los requisitos nacionales de Difusión Limitada y, sobre esta metodología nacional, obtuvo la acreditación NATO Restricted incorporando los requisitos de la Directiva 32 de la OTAN. Esto demuestra nuestro compromiso continuo de ayudar al sector público, a la defensa y a los clientes vinculados a la OTAN a ejecutar cargas de trabajo sensibles en la nube cumpliendo los requisitos de seguridad nacionales e internacionales más exigentes aplicables.</p><h2 id=\"sec-7\">Qué abarca</h2><p>La acreditación Difusión Limitada y NATO Restricted del CNI confirma que el sistema de AWS en la Región AWS Europa (España) cumple los requisitos procedimentales y de seguridad para tratar información clasificada hasta el nivel Difusión Limitada y NATO Restricted.</p><h2 id=\"sec-8\">¿Cuál es el marco español de información clasificada?</h2><p>El marco español de protección de la información clasificada nacional lo administran la ONS y el CCN, bajo el CNI. En 2026, España estableció el marco que permite tratar información Difusión Limitada en la nube pública comercial, en virtud del cual se ha concedido esta acreditación. La acreditación se basa en la <span><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/es/compliance/esquema-nacional-de-seguridad/\">certificación ENS categoría Alta</a></span> de AWS y en las cualificaciones del <span><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/es/compliance/ccn-stic/\">Catálogo de Productos y Servicios de Seguridad TIC</a></span> (CPSTIC) del CCN. El alcance de la acreditación incluye los servicios cualificados en CPSTIC y todos los servicios de AWS certificados en el ENS categoría Alta (consulte la <span><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/es/compliance/services-in-scope/ENS-High/\">lista de servicios de AWS en el alcance del ENS categoría Alta</a></span>). Solo pueden utilizarse para cargas de trabajo Difusión Limitada y NATO Restricted los servicios de este alcance cualificados o certificados en el marco del CCN (CPSTIC y ENS categoría Alta) que se ejecuten en la Región AWS Europa (España).</p><h2 id=\"sec-9\">¿Qué es NATO Restricted?</h2><p>La Directiva 32 de la OTAN establece los requisitos de seguridad para tratar información NATO Restricted en la nube pública, y es la directiva a la que hace referencia la política española <span><a href=\"https://www.ccn-cert.cni.es/es/guias-de-acceso-publico-ccn-stic/7358-ccn-stic-004-manejo-de-informacion-con-clasificacion-difusion-limitada-o-equivalente-en-nube-publica/file.html\">CCN-STIC-004</a></span>.</p><h2 id=\"sec-10\">Por qué es importante para los clientes</h2><p>Las organizaciones del sector público y de defensa en España pueden utilizar la Región AWS Europa (España) para cargas de trabajo clasificadas nacionales Difusión Limitada, así como para cargas de trabajo NATO Restricted. Conforme al modelo de responsabilidad compartida, los clientes que quieran tratar información clasificada en la Región AWS Europa (España) deben dirigirse al CCN y a la ONS para acreditar sus propios sistemas, apoyándose en la acreditación de AWS.</p><h2 id=\"sec-11\">Cómo empezar</h2><p>Los clientes de seguridad nacional y defensa pueden apoyarse en <span><a href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/solutions/trusted-secure-enclaves-on-aws/\">AWS Trusted Secure Enclave, Sensitive Edition (TSE-SE)</a></span> para diseñar una arquitectura cloud para sus cargas de trabajo sensibles. La documentación de la acreditación está disponible para los clientes elegibles a través de <span><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/es/artifact/\">AWS Artifact</a></span>. Los clientes también pueden trabajar con sus equipos de cuenta de AWS para entender cómo se aplican a sus casos de uso la acreditación Difusión Limitada y NATO Restricted y TSE-SE.</p><p>Para más información sobre el cumplimiento de AWS en España, consulte la <span><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/es/compliance/esquema-nacional-de-seguridad/\">página de cumplimiento ENS de AWS</a></span> y la página de <span><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/es/compliance/programs/\">Programas de cumplimiento de AWS</a></span>.</p><p>Para más detalles, consulte la página web de <span><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/dl-spain-and-nato-restricted-service-approval/\">AWS sobre NATO Restricted y Difusión Limitada para la Región AWS Europa (España)</a></span></p><p>If you have feedback about this post, submit comments in the Comments section below. If you have questions about this post, <span><a href=\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/support/home\">contact AWS Support</a></span>.</p><hr><p> \n   <img src=\"/dailyinfo/media/b3a52560513489d6.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Borja Larrumbide\" width=\"120\" height=\"160\"> \n  </p><h3 id=\"sec-12\">Borja Larrumbide</h3><p>Borja is a Security Assurance Manager for AWS in Iberia. He has a bachelor’s degree in computer science from Boston University (USA) and has worked in companies such as Microsoft and BBVA in different roles and sectors. Borja is a seasoned security assurance practitioner with many years of experience engaging key stakeholders at national and international levels. His areas of interest include security, privacy, risk management, and compliance. </p>","zhKind","complete","标准","合规","供应链","云原生","AWS","https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/security/aws-achieves-spains-national-limited-distribution-difusion-limitada-and-nato-restricted-accreditation-in-the-aws-europe-spain-region/","AWS Security Blog",{"_136":137,"_138":-5},"changelogVersion","2026-10-01T08:00","release"]
